\name{OneTriggersOtherOrder}
\alias{OneTriggersOtherOrder}
\title{An order that places a second, described in advance, once the first one fills}
\description{
The second order is sized to what the first actually filled, and grown as more of it fills, so a partial fill never leaves the second order larger than the position it follows. UBI builds the second order by laying the \code{then_} settings over the whole template, so a template \code{price} is carried into a \code{then_order_type} of \code{market} and refused; give such a template no price, or give the second order its own. UBI checks the second order before sending the first, so a dry run catches that. By default UBI holds a limit first order in its virtual order book until the other side of the book reaches its price, answering HTTP 202 with an \code{outcome} of \code{armed}, while the second order rests at the broker; give \code{hold_limits} \code{FALSE} to send the first order at once. If the second order has already finished when the first fills further, UBI sends a new second order for the extra quantity. A second order the broker refuses cancels the rest of the first, and the parent ends \code{failed}, because what the first filled is left without it.

The order template's attributes are described on \code{SyntheticOrder}.
}
